{"id":"eglon","name":"Eglon","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:eglon"],"groups":["1. King of Moab","2. An ancient city of Canaan"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eglon","text":"The bullock; place of heifers. (1.) Chieftain or king of one of the Moabite tribes (Judg. 3:12-14). Having entered into an alliance with Ammon and Amalek, he overran the trans-Jordanic region, and then crossing the Jordan, seized on Jericho, the “city of palm trees,” which had been by this time rebuilt, but not as a fortress. He made this city his capital, and kept Israel in subjection for eighteen years. The people at length “cried unto the Lord” in their distress, and he “raised them up a deliverer” in Ehud (q.v.), the son of Gera, a Benjamite. (2.) A city in Judah, near Lachish (Josh. 15:39). It was destroyed by Joshua (10:5, 6). It has been identified with Tell Nejileh, 6 miles south of Tell Hesy or Ajlan, north-west of Lachish. (See LACHISH.)"},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5700","lemma":"עֶגְלוֹן","xlit":"ʻEglôwn","gloss":"Eglon, the name of a place in Palestine and of a Moabitish king","kjv":"Eglon","count":6,"share":0.27},{"strong":"H5944","lemma":"עֲלִיָּה","xlit":"ʻălîyâh","gloss":"something lofty","kjv":"ascent, chamber, going up, loft","count":4,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H1817","lemma":"דֶּלֶת","xlit":"deleth","gloss":"something swinging","kjv":"door, gate, leaf, lid","count":3,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H4503","lemma":"מִנְחָה","xlit":"minchâh","gloss":"a donation","kjv":"gift, oblation, offering, present","count":3,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H2719","lemma":"חֶרֶב","xlit":"chereb","gloss":"drought","kjv":"axe, dagger, knife, mattock","count":4,"share":0.18},{"strong":"H5221","lemma":"נָכָה","xlit":"nâkâh","gloss":"to strike","kjv":"beat, cast forth, clap, give","count":3,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Josh.10.23","Josh.15.39","Judg.3.12","Judg.3.14","Judg.3.15","Judg.3.17","Josh.10.35","Judg.3.13","Judg.3.16","Judg.3.18","Judg.3.19","Judg.3.20","Judg.3.21","Judg.3.2